  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Compaction must not eat a collection.

 It used to keep ONE FACT PER KIND: it walked the log, dropped any entry whose
 kind it had already seen, and rewrote what was left. That is right for a kind
 holding a single current value -- the browser's history blob is rewritten
 whole, and only the newest matters -- and it destroys any kind holding a
 collection. Kind 24 is secret ENTRIES. Kind 25 is FileShare manifests. Kind 26
 is revocation records. Kind 30 is every source definition in the repository.

 So: write three distinct facts of kind 30, and one exact duplicate of the
 first. Compaction must keep the three, because nothing on the disk says one
 supersedes another, and it may collapse the duplicate, because the same kind
 and the same content hash IS the same fact. Under the old rule this test would
 report one survivor and two destroyed source files.

 The other half is order. The old walk collected survivors newest-first and
 rewrote the log in that order, so a compacted log came out REVERSED -- and
 app-scan-last, which trusts log order to mean recency, would then hand back
 the OLDEST fact of a kind. Survivors keep their log order here. The copy of
 alpha that survives is the newest one, so alpha ends up where that copy sat,
 which is last: beta, gamma, alpha.

Section: Entry

  kind-source : Integer = 30

  shown : Maybe Fact -> Text
  shown (m) =
   when m
    is Just (f) -> f.content
    is None -> "LOST"

  joined : List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  joined (xs) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else joined xs (i + 1) len (if i == 0 then list-at xs i else acc & "," & list-at xs i)

  opening : [Device.Block, Console.Write] Nothing = act
    let s0 = disk-init
    in let s1 = app-write-fact s0 kind-source "alpha" 1
    in let s2 = app-write-fact s1 kind-source "beta" 2
    in let s3 = app-write-fact s2 kind-source "gamma" 3
    in let s4 = app-write-fact s3 kind-source "alpha" 4
    in let flushed = disk-checkpoint s4
    in act
      print-line-uni ("written (alpha beta gamma alpha): " & show (disk-fact-count flushed))

      let packed = disk-compact flushed
      in act
        print-line-uni ("after compaction: " & show (disk-fact-count packed))
        let all = app-scan-all packed kind-source
        in print-line-uni ("survivors, in log order: " & joined all 0 (list-length all) "")

        let reloaded = disk-load
        in act
          print-line-uni ("alpha: " & shown (disk-read-fact reloaded (fact-content-hash "alpha")))
          print-line-uni ("beta:  " & shown (disk-read-fact reloaded (fact-content-hash "beta")))
          print-line-uni ("gamma: " & shown (disk-read-fact reloaded (fact-content-hash "gamma")))
        end
      end
    end
  end

